title: Campaigning
new-page: true
view-if: not rubicon or campaigning_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; campaigning_timer += 2 if rubicon
max-visits: 36
is-card: true
card-image: img/flags.jpg
frequency: 100
tags: party_affairs

= Campaigning

Whether or not we are in an electoral campaign, the party is always trying to broaden its voter base. Who should we focus our campaign efforts on?

- @new_middle: The "new" middle class, mostly government employees and white-collar workers, our traditional support base.
- @workers: The urban working class.
- @old_middle: The "old" middle class of small business owners.
- @rural: Rural workers and small farmers, who have historically been harmed by our environmental policies.
- @unemployed: The unemployed.
- @environmentalists: Environmentalists, who have historically voted for us.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@new_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: new_middle_egk += 10*(1-dissent); new_middle_egk -= 4 if socialism <= 49 and peoples_party == 0; resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1;

We have increased our campaigning among the new middle class. [? if socialism <= 49 and peoples_party == 0: The popular antipathy towards <span style="color: #30B24A;">socialism</span> among this group makes our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?]

@workers
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: workers_egk += 5*(1-dissent); new_middle_egk += 5*(1-dissent); old_middle_egk += 5*(1-dissent); rural_egk += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_egk += 5*(1-dissent); workers_egk -= 1 if unemployed >= 20; workers_egk -= 1 if unemployed >= 30; workers_egk += 5*(1-dissent) if wtb_adopted = 1; resources -= 1; workers_egk += 30*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress >= 1;

We have increased our campaigning among the workers. [? if unemployed >= 15: The high levels of unemployment make our campaign more difficult. ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract workers. ?]

@old_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: old_middle_egk += 5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; old_middle_egk -= 3 if nationalism >= 51 and peoples_party == 0; peoples_party_support += 1

We have increased our campaigning among the old middle class. [? if nationalism >= 51 and peoples_party == 0: The high levels of nationalism among this group make our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?]

@rural
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: rural_egk += 5*(1-dissent); rural_egk -= 3*(1-dissent) if peoples_party == 0; resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1; rural_egk += 3*(1-dissent) if rural_policy >= 2

We have increased our campaigning among farmers. [? if peoples_party == 0: We have not historically campaigned much among the farmers, and they do not trust us. ?][? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among farmers than before. ?][? if rural_policy >= 2 : Our rural policies have made it easier for us to build support among farmers. ?]

@unemployed
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: unemployed_egk += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; unemployed_egk -= 3 if welfare < 0; unemployed_egk -= 2 if unemployed >= 30; unemployed_egk += 6*(1-dissent) if wtb_adopted = 1; unemployed_egk += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare >= 2;

We have increased our campaigning among the unemployed. [? if welfare < 0: The welfare cuts and resultant poverty make our campaign more difficult, since we are associated with the government that enacted these cuts, and our campaign may even backfire. ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract support from the unemployed. ?]

@environmentalists
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: peoples_party == 1
on-arrival: catholics_egk += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1

We have increased our campaigning among Environmentalists.
